# Build-time options for instrument.sh and fetch.sh.  Copy to
# src/instrumentrc -- without the .example -- and rebuild the image; the file
# is sourced as bash, inside the container, before either script decides
# anything.
#
# It exists because captain forwards a fixed set of --build-args and this
# fuzzer would otherwise need a change to the shared docker/Dockerfile to be
# told anything at build time.

# Which branch of github.com/r-fuzz/symsan fetch.sh clones.  campaign.sh writes
# this from --branch; set by hand only when running fetch.sh/build.sh outside
# of campaign.sh.
#SYMSAN_BRANCH=main

# Build the coverage side with afl-clang-lto and AFL_LLVM_DOCUMENT_IDS, and
# both sides with -g, so symsan-fuzz can join SymSan's branch ids to AFL++'s
# edge ids and skip solving branches the fuzzer has already covered.
#
# Off by default.  It needs LTO, debug info on both builds, and a map named
# <executable>.map, and it degrades *silently* without any of them: a wrong map
# reports a high mapped-branch ratio while telling the concolic stage that
# everything is already covered.  Turn it on deliberately, then audit it with
# covcheck and --validate-branch-map (see bindings/rust/README.md).
#
# Refused outright on targets that build more than one program -- LTO numbers
# edges per link, so one document-ids file cannot describe two of them.
#USE_BRANCH_MAP=1

# Skip the cmplog build.  The baseline arm costs one extra build and nothing at
# run time if unused, so the default is on.
#USE_CMPLOG=0

# Skip the concolic build, giving the havoc floor: LibAFL's scheduler and
# mutators over the coverage build, with no extra stage.  Set USE_CMPLOG=0 too
# for a bare floor, or leave it on for cmplog-only.
#
# Unlike the other two this changes what run.sh is *allowed* to do, so it also
# leaves $OUT/no_symsan in the image: a missing concolic binary is otherwise
# indistinguishable from a build that failed, and run.sh refuses to start rather
# than measure the floor under the name of the symsan arm.
#
# Incompatible with USE_BRANCH_MAP, whose only consumer is the concolic stage.
#USE_SYMSAN=0
